# --- Private working material -------------------------------------------
# Design docs, the execution plan, and the AI working instructions used to
# build Sentinel. Kept in the working tree, deliberately never published.
# Anything a user or contributor needs is in README.md and docs/ instead.
product-docs/
CLAUDE.md

# Internal build notes that sit next to the code they describe, so they are
# ignored in place rather than moved. Neither is something a user needs:
# `assets/` explains how the icons were generated, `plugins/` explains the
# crate layout — CONTRIBUTING.md carries the part a contributor actually needs.
assets/README.md
plugins/README.md

# Claude Code local state (machine-specific permissions, session data)
.claude/

# --- Rust ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output lands at the workspace root: core/ and src-tauri/ share one
# workspace, so it is not inside src-tauri/target.
/target

# --- Node / frontend -----------------------------------------------------
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# --- Packaging output ----------------------------------------------------
# Release bundles are attached to GitHub Releases by CI, never committed.
*.AppImage
*.deb
*.rpm

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# Tauri updater signing keys especially: a leaked private key lets someone
# else sign an update your users would install. Keep it in GitHub Secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# --- Editors and OS ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
